{"task": "Prove exactly this local conditional obligation using the supplied NL route. Return only the tactic body through submit_transition. All displayed parameter and input proof binders are already in context.", "packet": {"version": 2, "contract_sha256": "3575d5d75c1eb2aaf8b92e3182b02e09afba2fd0f4d1ab9e569e2cc16c872495", "header": "import Mathlib

open scoped ENNReal NNReal BigOperators

abbrev YuiEucl (n : ℕ) := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)
def YuiI : Set ℝ := Set.Icc 0 1
def YuiSnoc {n : ℕ} (x : YuiEucl n) (t : ℝ) : YuiEucl (n + 1) :=
  WithLp.toLp 2 (Fin.snoc (fun i => x i) t)
def YuiHead {n : ℕ} (z : YuiEucl (n + 1)) : YuiEucl n :=
  WithLp.toLp 2 (fun i : Fin n => z i.castSucc)
def YuiLast {n : ℕ} (z : YuiEucl (n + 1)) : ℝ := z (Fin.last n)
def YuiCylinder {n : ℕ} (E : Set (YuiEucl n)) : Set (YuiEucl (n + 1)) :=
  {z | YuiHead z ∈ E ∧ YuiLast z ∈ YuiI}
noncomputable def YuiCost {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X] {ι : Type*}
    (s : ℝ) (U : ι → Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ∑' i, ⨆ (_ : (U i).Nonempty), (Metric.ediam (U i)) ^ s
def YuiCover {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X] (δ : ℝ) (A : Set X)
    (U : ℕ → Set X) : Prop :=
  A ⊆ ⋃ i, U i ∧ ∀ i, Metric.ediam (U i) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal δ
noncomputable def YuiContent {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X]
    (s δ : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ⨅ (U : ℕ → Set X) (_ : YuiCover δ A U), YuiCost s U
noncomputable def YuiMeasure {X : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace X]
    (s : ℝ) (A : Set X) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ⨆ (δ : ℝ) (_ : 0 < δ), YuiContent s δ A
", "parameters": [{"name": "n", "type": "ℕ"}, {"name": "E", "type": "Set (YuiEucl n)"}], "representation": "Use EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)=PiLp 2 (constant ℝ), indexed by Fin n, with its native L2 metric and Borel structure; n is a natural ambient dimension including 0. YuiSnoc appends a real coordinate and YuiHead/YuiLast recover it; YuiCylinder E is defined by these coordinates directly in EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n+1)). T003 checks the coordinate inverse and Euclidean distance identities used by all cylinder arguments, so there is no max-product metric or unproved metric replacement. The interval remains Set.Icc (0:ℝ) 1. Metric.ediam, YuiCost, YuiContent and YuiMeasure take values in ℝ≥0∞; ^ with a real exponent is ENNReal.rpow. The supremum over a nonempty witness equals ediam^s and over an empty witness equals zero, giving the prescribed empty-cover convention even at exponent zero. All uses of Hausdorff content or normalization are guarded by s>0 and δ>0. Cover sequences enumerate countable covers with empty padding; the positive-diameter construction uses a subset of ℕ to avoid duplicating finite nonempty families. dimH is native, defined as the supremum of nonnegative exponents with infinite native unnormalized Hausdorff measure; its nonnegative extended codomain gives dimH empty=0. Positive real exponents are embedded by ENNReal.ofReal only with the relevant positivity; D remains dimH E in ℝ≥0∞ and its toReal value is used only downstream of T005's finiteness. Nat casts of n and constants are finite ENNReal values. Lebesgue measure/integrals in the slicing and interval workers are volume on ℝ and the nonnegative lintegral. All five M facts are supplied by direct pinned Mathlib use, not additional premises. Background notes remain optional node-local references. N outputs are unchanged; auxiliary T001 exposes the uniform metric-space normalization calculation already used in S001 so both Euclidean and real-interval instances can share it.", "inputs": [], "target": "∀ k : ℕ, (∀ (x : YuiEucl k) (t : ℝ), YuiHead (YuiSnoc x t) = x ∧ YuiLast (YuiSnoc x t) = t) ∧ (∀ z : YuiEucl (k + 1), YuiSnoc (YuiHead z) (YuiLast z) = z) ∧ (∀ (x y : YuiEucl k) (t u : ℝ), dist (YuiSnoc x t) (YuiSnoc y u) = Real.sqrt ((dist x y) ^ 2 + |t-u| ^ 2)) ∧ LipschitzWith 1 (YuiHead (n := k)) ∧ LipschitzWith 1 (YuiLast (n := k))", "explanation": "Shared coordinate implementation facts already used by the accepted product-distance calculations. Fin n indexes the first n coordinates; Fin.last n is the appended coordinate. Fin.snoc, head and last are inverse point constructions including n=0. EuclideanSpace is PiLp 2, so EuclideanSpace.dist_eq/dist_sq_eq split the finite sum into the first n squares and the last square. The numeral 2 is the L2 exponent, not a coordinate count or max-product norm; LipschitzWith 1 uses a nonnegative real Lipschitz constant. These identities justify the two coordinate diameter bounds and the fixed-x interval embedding.", "source_steps": [{"id": "S012", "text": "Choose U from F002; set r_i=diam(U_i) and N_i=ceil(1/r_i). Partition I into N_i equal closed intervals of length 1/N_i≤r_i. Since 0<r_i≤r≤1, N_i≤1/r_i+1≤2/r_i. Let W be the family of products of U_i with these intervals. It is countable, being a countable union of finite families, and covers F. For any two points in a member of W, the squared Euclidean distance is at most r_i^2+r_i^2. Thus each member has diameter ≤sqrt(2) r_i≤sqrt(2) r."}, {"id": "S016", "text": "Fix s>0 and delta>0. Take any countable family V and introduce L1: V is a delta-cover of F. Enumerate it with possible empty padding, discard empties, and write T⊆N for the remaining indices; all i-series in this inference are over T. Define rho_i=diam(V_i), and A_i and B_i as its first and last coordinate projections. By the Euclidean distance formula, each coordinate projection is 1-Lipschitz. Thus A_i and B_i are nonempty and have diameter ≤rho_i≤delta. In particular B_i is bounded, with finite infimum and supremum and sup B_i-inf B_i≤rho_i. Put c=H^s_delta(E). By N002, c is finite."}, {"id": "S030", "text": "H002 supplies a point x0∈E. Define g:I→Eucl(n+1) by g(t)=(x0,t). The Euclidean distance between g(t) and g(u) is sqrt(0+|t-u|^2)=|t-u|, so g preserves distances. Its image is contained in F by x0∈E and the definition F=E×I. N001 gives dimH(g(I))=dimH(I) and dimH(F)≥dimH(g(I)). N006 gives dimH(I)=1, hence dimH(F)≥1. Under the temporary premise L1: D=0, this reads dimH(F)≥1=D+1. Discharge L1; x0 is absent from the output. This proves the exported claim for all n, including n=0."}], "boundary": "Only listed inputs are project premises. The pinned Mathlib environment is freely available; no sibling proof is supplied.", "background_supplement_sha256": "1bf0b9c7347572e230e12960e1ad72681eb160b097abdd7fb42c849256a378a3", "objects": [], "representations": [], "bridges": [], "shared_inputs": [], "background_note_index": [{"id": "R003.BG004", "at": "/inference/argument/2/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fact": "For 0<t≤1, the integer m=ceil(1/t) is positive and satisfies 1/m≤t and m≤1/t+1≤2/t. A countable union of finite families is countable. If diam U=t and J is an interval of length at most t, then the Euclidean product U×J has diameter at most sqrt(2)t."}, {"id": "R004.BG001", "at": "/inference/argument/0/text", "kind": "mathematical", "fact": "If V is a nonempty subset of Eucl(n)×R with finite diameter rho, both coordinate projections are nonempty and have diameter at most rho. Its last-coordinate image B is bounded and has real infimum and supremum with sup B−inf B≤rho."}, {"id": "R007.BG001", "at": "/inference/argument/0/text", "kind": "elementary", "fact": "For real t,u, sqrt(0+|t-u|^2)=|t-u|."}]}}
